# Line endings are load-bearing in this repo, not cosmetic:
#
#   - hooks/*.sh are executed by /bin/sh. A CRLF shebang makes the interpreter
#     look for "/bin/sh\r" and the hook fails to run at all.
#   - scripts/validate-plugin.ts parses frontmatter by matching a literal
#     "---\n", so a CRLF checkout fails every skill, command and agent.
#
# CI runs on ubuntu and never sees either problem. Pinning LF here keeps a
# Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true) able to run `bun run validate` and
# `bun test` locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ts   text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

bun.lock text eol=lf
